ution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#jsx-runtime-modes\",\"content\":\"**`runtime: \\\"preact\\\"`** — uses Preact's automatic JSX transform (`jsxRuntime`) and should be treated as the trusted browser source lane\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-56\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-56\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#jsx-runtime-modes\",\"content\":\"**`runtime: \\\"renderify\\\"`** — uses custom `__renderify_runtime_h()` that produces RuntimeNode objects\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-57\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-57\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#import-rewriting\",\"content\":\"After transpilation, `es-module-lexer` extracts all import specifiers. Each bare specifier is resolved to a full CDN URL, and the source is rewritten with the resolved URLs. The final source is loaded via a `blob:` URL with `dynamic import()`.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-58\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-58\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#module-graph-materialization\",\"content\":\"For complex source modules with transitive dependencies, the runtime materializes the full module graph:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-59\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-59\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#module-graph-materialization\",\"content\":\"Each module is fetched, its imports are recursively rewritten, and it's stored as a blob URL. This solves the browser limitation where bare specifiers are not supported in native ESM.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-60\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-60\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#module-graph-materialization\",\"content\":\"Browser Preact singleton imports are the controlled exception: same-origin\\ninstalled Preact paths and recognized Preact CDN package paths remain native so\\nhooks share one runtime instance. Before returning a native URL, Renderify\\nfetches and recursively audits its graph against module budgets, response-size\\nlimits, redirects, and network policy. Preact-looking paths on other origins\\nare materialized normally.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-61\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-61\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#standard-default\",\"content\":\"Source executes in the main page context. No isolation.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-62\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-62\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#isolated-vm\",\"content\":\"This profile is reserved for a future secure component-isolation backend. The current runtime does not use Node's `node:vm` as a security boundary: host objects can expose paths back into the host realm, and loading a component before entering a VM already executes its module-level code outside the boundary.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-63\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-63\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#isolated-vm\",\"content\":\"By default, requesting `isolated-vm` produces `RUNTIME_ISOLATION_UNAVAILABLE` and stops before dependency preflight, import loading, or component module loading. `probePlan()` follows the same rule.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-64\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-64\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#isolated-vm\",\"content\":\"Trusted callers may opt into compatibility behavior with `allowIsolationFallback: true`. This emits `RUNTIME_ISOLATION_FALLBACK`, changes the effective profile to `standard`, and allows both module initialization and component code to run without isolation. Never enable this fallback for untrusted modules.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-65\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-65\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#sandbox-worker\",\"content\":\"Source code executes in a Web Worker. The worker has a configurable timeout and communicates results via `postMessage`. If execution exceeds the timeout, the worker is terminated.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-66\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-66\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#sandbox-iframe\",\"content\":\"This compatibility profile routes source code through the same terminable Web\\nWorker boundary as `sandbox-worker`. Renderify does not execute untrusted source\\ninside an iframe because a synchronous loop there cannot be reliably stopped by\\na main-thread timer. If Worker execution is unavailable, the profile fails\\nclosed.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-67\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-67\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#sandbox-shadowrealm\",\"content\":\"This compatibility profile also routes source code through a terminable Web\\nWorker. A `ShadowRealm` is same-thread and cannot provide a reliable synchronous\\ntermination boundary. Availability of the `ShadowRealm` API therefore does not\\nchange execution routing; without Worker support, execution fails closed.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-68\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-68\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#sandbox-shadowrealm\",\"content\":\"Browser sandbox execution profiles apply to declarative plans and `source.runtime: \\\"renderify\\\"` modules. `source.runtime: \\\"preact\\\"` stays on the trusted in-page lane and does not use worker, iframe, or ShadowRealm sandbox adapters.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-69\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-69\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#sandbox-shadowrealm\",\"content\":\"For explicit `sandbox-worker`, `sandbox-iframe`, and `sandbox-shadowrealm`\\nexecution profiles, sandbox failure is always terminal. Setting\\n`browserSourceSandboxFailClosed: false` does not permit an unsafe same-thread\\nfallback for those profiles. Requesting one of these browser-only profiles in a\\nnon-browser runtime fails with `RUNTIME_ISOLATION_UNAVAILABLE` before dependency\\nor source loading begins.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-70\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-70\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"The runtime tracks three budget dimensions during execution:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-71\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-71\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Budget\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-72\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-72\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"What It Tracks\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-73\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-73\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"What Happens When Exceeded\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-74\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-74\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Import budget\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-75\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-75\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Declared imports and distinct remote materializations\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-76\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-76\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Execution stops, diagnostic emitted\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-77\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-77\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Component budget\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-78\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-78\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Number of component node renders\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-79\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-79\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Execution stops, diagnostic emitted\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-80\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-80\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Time budget\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-81\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-81\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Wall-clock execution time\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-82\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-82\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Execution stops, diagnostic emitted\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-83\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-83\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#execution-budgets\",\"content\":\"Budgets are configured via `plan.capabilities`:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-84\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-84\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#dependency-preflight\",\"content\":\"Before execution, the runtime can probe all required modules to verify availability:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-85\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-85\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#dependency-preflight\",\"content\":\"Preflight checks:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-86\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-86\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#dependency-preflight\",\"content\":\"`plan.imports` specifiers\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-87\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-87\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#dependency-preflight\",\"content\":\"Component node modules\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-88\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-88\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#dependency-preflight\",\"content\":\"Source code imports\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-89\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-89\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#dependency-preflight\",\"content\":\"Configuration:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-90\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-90\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#remote-fetch-configuration\",\"content\":\"Module fetching supports retry, timeout, and CDN fallback:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-91\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-91\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#remote-fetch-configuration\",\"content\":\"The runtime issues hedged fetch attempts across the primary URL and configured fallback CDNs. The first successful response wins.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-92\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-92\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#remote-fetch-configuration\",\"content\":\"To force JSPM-only behavior (no fallback CDNs) in strict deployments:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-93\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-93\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#remote-fetch-configuration\",\"content\":\"This preset also forces strict security profile, module manifest/integrity checks, and preflight fail-fast.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-94\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-94\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#state-management\",\"content\":\"The runtime maintains per-plan state snapshots:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-95\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-95\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#state-management\",\"content\":\"State is initialized from `plan.state.initial` on first execution. Subsequent executions preserve state across renders.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-96\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-96\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#declarative-transitions\",\"content\":\"State transitions are defined in `plan.state.transitions` and triggered by runtime events:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-97\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-97\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#template-interpolation\",\"content\":\"Text nodes support template interpolation with double-brace syntax:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-98\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-98\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#template-interpolation\",\"content\":\"Interpolation resolves against the current execution context, including state, context variables, and event payloads.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-99\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-99\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#verification-model\",\"content\":\"Renderify validates third-party TSX/JSX dependencies through a layered runtime model rather than a single static check:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-100\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-100\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#verification-model\",\"content\":\"**Lexical import extraction** — source imports are parsed via `es-module-lexer` (with fallback parser), not plain regex string scanning.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-101\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-101\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#verification-model\",\"content\":\"**Specifier normalization + rejection** — `JspmModuleLoader` resolves bare specifiers to JSPM URLs and rejects Node.js builtins and unsupported schemes.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-102\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-102\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#verification-model\",\"content\":\"**Policy gate** — security policy checks module hosts, bare-specifier manifest coverage, and (in strict mode) integrity requirements for remote modules.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-103\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-103\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#verification-model\",\"content\":\"**Integrity verification** — when `moduleManifest[*].integrity` is provided, runtime fetches module content and verifies the digest before execution.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-104\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-104\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#verification-model\",\"content\":\"**Dependency preflight** — runtime can probe all dependency edges before execution; with fail-fast enabled, render aborts on preflight errors.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-105\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-105\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#verification-model\",\"content\":\"**Executable ESM validation** — dependencies are fetched, rewritten, and dynamically imported in the real runtime path; failures are surfaced as runtime diagnostics.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-106\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-106\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#verification-model\",\"content\":\"This design intentionally treats dependency validity as **runtime-verifiable evidence** instead of compile-time assumption.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-107\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-107\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#render-artifacts\",\"content\":\"When a source module produces a Preact component, the runtime emits a `renderArtifact`:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-108\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-108\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#render-artifacts\",\"content\":\"The UI renderer uses this artifact for Preact-native rendering with full reconciliation support, rather than falling back to HTML string conversion.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-109\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-109\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#abort-support\",\"content\":\"All runtime operations accept an `AbortSignal`:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-110\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-110\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#abort-support\",\"content\":\"When aborted:\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-111\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-111\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#abort-support\",\"content\":\"In-progress module fetches are cancelled\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-112\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-112\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#abort-support\",\"content\":\"Worker sandbox execution is terminated\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-execution-113\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution-113\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-execution\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-execution#abort-support\",\"content\":\"An `AbortError` is thrown\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"RuntimePlan IR\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"Documentation\",\"Runtime\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir-0\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir-0\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir\",\"content\":\"Canonical RuntimePlan nodes, capabilities, state transitions, templates, imports, and source modules.\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir-1\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir-1\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir#runtimeplan-ir-reference\",\"content\":\"RuntimePlan IR Reference\"}],[\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir-2\",{\"id\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir-2\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/runtime-plan-ir\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"