urity\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#2-module-specifier-validation\",\"content\":\"Module specifiers are validated against the allowlist:\"}],[\"/docs/security-185\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-185\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#3-capability-budget-enforcement\",\"content\":\"Plan capabilities are validated against policy limits:\"}],[\"/docs/security-186\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-186\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#3-capability-budget-enforcement\",\"content\":\"The same `maxAllowedImports` policy also caps the number of entries accepted in\\n`moduleManifest`, so an unused or alias-heavy manifest cannot bypass the\\npolicy's import resource ceiling.\"}],[\"/docs/security-187\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-187\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#4-state-path-safety\",\"content\":\"All state paths are checked for prototype pollution:\"}],[\"/docs/security-188\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-188\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#5-runtime-source-analysis\",\"content\":\"Source code undergoes static analysis:\"}],[\"/docs/security-189\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-189\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#5-runtime-source-analysis\",\"content\":\"**Size limit** — source byte count must be within `maxRuntimeSourceBytes`\"}],[\"/docs/security-190\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-190\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#5-runtime-source-analysis\",\"content\":\"**Import count** — source import specifiers must be within `maxSourceImportSpecifiers`\"}],[\"/docs/security-191\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-191\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#5-runtime-source-analysis\",\"content\":\"**Banned patterns** — regex patterns matched against source (e.g., `eval()`, `fetch()`)\"}],[\"/docs/security-192\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-192\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#5-runtime-source-analysis\",\"content\":\"**Dynamic imports** — `import()` expressions are blocked unless explicitly allowed\"}],[\"/docs/security-193\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-193\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#5-runtime-source-analysis\",\"content\":\"**Manifest coverage** — bare import specifiers must have manifest entries (when required)\"}],[\"/docs/security-194\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-194\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#6-module-manifest-verification\",\"content\":\"In strict profile:\"}],[\"/docs/security-195\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-195\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#6-module-manifest-verification\",\"content\":\"Strict integrity coverage applies to every executable module reference in\\n`plan.imports`, component nodes, `capabilities.allowedModules`, and static\\nsource imports. Bare specifiers require an exact-key manifest entry. Direct\\nHTTP(S) references also require an exact-key entry whose `resolvedUrl` matches\\nthe referenced URL, so a URL cannot bypass manifest enforcement.\"}],[\"/docs/security-196\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-196\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#6-module-manifest-verification\",\"content\":\"Remote descriptors must provide at least one syntactically valid `sha256`,\\n`sha384`, or `sha512` SRI token. Missing entries, mismatched direct-URL targets,\\nmissing hashes, and unsupported hash formats generate policy violations. The\\nruntime separately verifies the declared digest against loaded module content.\"}],[\"/docs/security-197\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-197\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#ui-renderer-security\",\"content\":\"The UI renderer provides additional XSS protection beyond the policy checker (including light DOM + shadow DOM subtree sanitization):\"}],[\"/docs/security-198\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-198\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#blocked-tags-at-render-time\",\"content\":\"Even if a tag passes the policy check, the renderer blocks: `script`, `style`, `iframe`, `object`, `embed`, `link`, `meta`, `base`, `form`.\"}],[\"/docs/security-199\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-199\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#blocked-tags-at-render-time\",\"content\":\"Blocked tags are rendered as: `<div data-renderify-sanitized-tag=\\\"script\\\"></div>`\"}],[\"/docs/security-200\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-200\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#blocked-tags-at-render-time\",\"content\":\"`form` nodes are the one exception: they render as inert\\n`<div data-renderify-form>` containers that keep their children but drop\\n`action`, `method`, `target`, and `enctype`, and the runtime emulates\\n`onSubmit` from submit buttons and Enter. Real `<form>` elements never reach\\nthe DOM, so plan content cannot navigate the host or post fields to another\\norigin. Password and file inputs are never read into state, event payloads,\\nor submitted fields.\"}],[\"/docs/security-201\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-201\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#blocked-tags-at-render-time\",\"content\":\"This render-time tag sanitization applies to the declarative RuntimeNode path. `source.runtime: \\\"preact\\\"` renders through Preact directly and should be treated as trusted source output instead of relying on RuntimeNode tag sanitization. To run model-written source without trusting it, render it in a `@renderify/frame` sandbox instead.\"}],[\"/docs/security-202\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-202\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#attribute-sanitization\",\"content\":\"**Event handlers** — valid declarative bindings such as\\n`onClick: \\\"increment\\\"` or `onClick: { type: \\\"increment\\\", payload: {...} }`\\nbecome delegated RuntimeEvents and never become HTML attributes or evaluated\\ncode. Malformed/lowercase `on*` values are rejected or stripped. IR,\\nsecurity, and runtime share `parseRuntimeEventBinding` so validation and\\nrendering use the same grammar.\"}],[\"/docs/security-203\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-203\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#attribute-sanitization\",\"content\":\"**URL validation** — request-capable attributes such as `href`, `src`,\\n`srcset`, `ping`, `action`, `poster`, legacy media attributes, and SVG\\nfunctional IRIs reject active protocols and are checked against the security\\npolicy's network allowlist. The declarative renderer fails closed after\\ntemplate resolution: it emits only relative URLs plus `mailto:` and `tel:`\\non link attributes, so interpolated context or state cannot turn an\\nattribute into a cross-origin request.\"}],[\"/docs/security-204\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-204\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#attribute-sanitization\",\"content\":\"**Style validation** — inline `style` values are checked for XSS patterns:\"}],[\"/docs/security-205\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-205\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#attribute-sanitization\",\"content\":\"`expression()`\"}],[\"/docs/security-206\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-206\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#attribute-sanitization\",\"content\":\"`javascript:`\"}],[\"/docs/security-207\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-207\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#attribute-sanitization\",\"content\":\"`data:` (non-image)\"}],[\"/docs/security-208\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-208\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#attribute-sanitization\",\"content\":\"`@import`\"}],[\"/docs/security-209\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-209\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#attribute-sanitization\",\"content\":\"`url()` (blocked in render layer for defense-in-depth)\"}],[\"/docs/security-210\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-210\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#attribute-sanitization\",\"content\":\"CSS escape obfuscation patterns\"}],[\"/docs/security-211\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-211\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#attribute-sanitization\",\"content\":\"Null byte injection\"}],[\"/docs/security-212\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-212\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#link-safety\",\"content\":\"Links with `target=\\\"_blank\\\"` automatically receive `rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"` to prevent reverse tabnapping.\"}],[\"/docs/security-213\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-213\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#jspm-only-strict-mode-preset\",\"content\":\"For production deployments that require deterministic supplier boundaries, enable:\"}],[\"/docs/security-214\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-214\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#jspm-only-strict-mode-preset\",\"content\":\"This preset enforces:\"}],[\"/docs/security-215\",{\"id\":\"/docs/security-215\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/security\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/security#jspm-only-strict-mode-preset\",\"content\":\"security profile = `strict`\"}],[\"/docs/security-21