ry#amendment-opt-in-source-tier\",\"content\":\"Amendment: opt-in source tier\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-13\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-13\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#supersedes--superseded-by\",\"content\":\"Supersedes / Superseded by\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-14\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-14\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#context\",\"content\":\"An MCP App view receives data selected by a model and runs in a host-managed\\niframe. A handwritten JSON-RPC bridge is easy to make subtly incompatible, and\\nallowing Renderify source or CDN modules would make host CSP behavior part of\\nthe execution contract.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-15\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-15\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#context\",\"content\":\"The adapter must be useful without claiming that source scanning or a host's\\noptional sandbox behavior is a complete code-execution boundary.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-16\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-16\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#decision\",\"content\":\"The first `@renderify/mcp-app` release MUST:\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-17\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-17\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#decision\",\"content\":\"use `@modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps` for view and server protocol behavior;\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-18\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-18\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#decision\",\"content\":\"ship one self-contained, hash-CSP HTML resource;\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-19\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-19\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#decision\",\"content\":\"accept only offline `runtime-plan/v1` element/text trees;\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-20\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-20\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#decision\",\"content\":\"validate the plan on server and view sides;\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-21\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-21\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#decision\",\"content\":\"deny app-to-tool calls unless the exact tool is configured; and\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-22\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-22\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#decision\",\"content\":\"keep source, component modules, imports, external domains, timers, storage,\\nand alternate execution profiles outside the contract.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-23\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-23\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#handwritten-protocol-bridge\",\"content\":\"Rejected. It duplicates initialization, notification, request/response,\\ncapability, source-validation, and teardown behavior already maintained by the\\nofficial SDK. Protocol-shaped mocks can hide incompatibilities.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-24\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-24\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#declarative-and-arbitrary-source-in-one-package\",\"content\":\"Rejected for the initial release. Source execution requires a materially wider\\nCSP and a stronger isolation story. Static banned-pattern scans are not a hard\\nboundary for arbitrary JavaScript.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-25\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-25\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#declarative-shell-with-optional-cdn-mode\",\"content\":\"Rejected for the initial release. Optional external domains weaken portability\\nand make a server configuration change alter the trust boundary.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-26\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-26\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#offline-declarative-only-shell\",\"content\":\"Accepted. It preserves local state and structured interactivity while keeping\\ncode and network out of untrusted tool results.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-27\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-27\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#consequences\",\"content\":\"Hosts receive a deterministic resource with no external origins.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-28\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-28\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#consequences\",\"content\":\"Server authors cannot use React/Preact component modules through this adapter.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-29\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-29\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#consequences\",\"content\":\"Interactive server actions require explicit tool allowlisting and normal\\nserver authorization.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-30\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-30\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#consequences\",\"content\":\"Protocol upgrades largely follow the official dependency, but dependency\\nupdates still require conformance tests.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-31\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-31\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#consequences\",\"content\":\"A future source-capable tier is a separate security decision, not a flag added\\nto this one.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-32\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-32\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#risks\",\"content\":\"The official SDK and Renderify runtime are part of the trusted computing base.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-33\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-33\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#risks\",\"content\":\"Declarative UI can still mislead users or cause repeated local work.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-34\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-34\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#risks\",\"content\":\"Model-context and tool arguments remain attacker-influenced data.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-35\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-35\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#risks\",\"content\":\"Hosts may implement weaker iframe policies than the test host; the package\\ncannot enforce the outer sandbox.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-36\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-36\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#follow-up\",\"content\":\"Maintain the official-bridge browser conformance test.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-37\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-37\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#follow-up\",\"content\":\"Keep dependency and threat-model docs synchronized with any accepted surface\\nchange.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-38\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-38\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#follow-up\",\"content\":\"Require a new ADR before adding source execution or external domains.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-39\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-39\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#amendment-opt-in-source-tier\",\"content\":\"ADR-0002 is the separate security decision\\nthis record asked for before source execution. It adds an opt-in tier rather\\nthan changing this contract:\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-40\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-40\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#amendment-opt-in-source-tier\",\"content\":\"Apps registered without `sourceMode` are unchanged: offline plans, no\\nexternal origins, and a view that rejects source payloads.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-41\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-41\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#amendment-opt-in-source-tier\",\"content\":\"An app registered with `sourceMode: true` serves a different resource. It\\ndeclares its module CDNs in `_meta.ui.csp`, so hosts see the wider surface\\nbefore rendering, and it runs source only in a sandboxed frame nested in the\\nview, never in the view's window.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-42\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-42\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#amendment-opt-in-source-tier\",\"content\":\"Tool calls from source go through the same exact-name allowlist as\\ndeclarative events.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-43\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary-43\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0001-offline-declarative-mcp-app-boundary#supersedes--superseded-by\",\"content\":\"Amended by ADR-0002 (opt-in source tier).\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"ADR-0002 Sandboxed source frame\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"Documentation\",\"Project\",\"Decision records\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-0\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-0\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"content\":\"Run model-written source in an opaque-origin iframe owned by the SDK, including, when an MCP App opts in, inside its view.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-1\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-1\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#adr-0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"content\":\"ADR-0002: Sandboxed source frame\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-2\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-2\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#context\",\"content\":\"Context\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-3\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-3\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#decision\",\"content\":\"Decision\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-4\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-4\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#options-considered\",\"content\":\"Options considered\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-5\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-5\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#trusted-in-page-source\",\"content\":\"Trusted in-page source\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-6\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-6\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#web-worker-sandbox\",\"content\":\"Web Worker sandbox\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-7\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-7\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#dedicated-sandbox-origin\",\"content\":\"Dedicated sandbox origin\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-8\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-8\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#opaque-origin-srcdoc-frame\",\"content\":\"Opaque-origin `srcdoc` frame\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-9\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-9\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#mcp-source-mode\",\"content\":\"MCP source mode\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-10\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-10\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#consequences\",\"content\":\"Consequences\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-11\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-11\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#follow-up\",\"content\":\"Follow-up\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-12\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-12\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#supersedes--superseded-by\",\"content\":\"Supersedes / Superseded by\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-13\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-13\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#context\",\"content\":\"Declarative RuntimePlans cover forms, lists, and conditions, but open-ended\\nrequests (\\\"a chart with this npm library\\\", \\\"a kanban board with drag and drop\\\")\\nneed model-written JSX or TSX. Until now the only way to run that source\\ninteractively was the `trusted` profile, which executes it in the host page\\nwith the host's privileges. Static source scanning is not an isolation\\nboundary.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-14\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-14\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#context\",\"content\":\"The website Playground already ran source in a `sandbox=\\\"allow-scripts\\\"`\\niframe with a restrictive CSP and a MessagePort protocol. Hosts asked for the\\nsame isolation without copying the Playground's code. Two weaknesses had to be\\nfixed on the way: the Playground runner accepted a connection from any window\\nthat could post to it, and a synchronous infinite loop could freeze the host,\\nbecause many browsers run an opaque-origin iframe on the embedding page's\\nthread, where no watchdog timer can fire.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-15\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-15\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#decision\",\"content\":\"Ship `@renderify/frame` as the supported way to run untrusted source and plans\\nin a browser. A frame MUST:\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-16\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-16\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#decision\",\"content\":\"be an `<iframe sandbox=\\\"allow-scripts\\\">` without `allow-same-origin` or any\\nother sandbox token, so content has an opaque origin and cannot read the host\\nDOM, cookies, or storage, submit forms, open popups, or navigate the top\\nwindow;\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-17\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-17\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#decision\",\"content\":\"load its document from `srcdoc` with a CSP of `default-src 'none'`, scripts\\nonly from the runner's origin, the configured module CDNs, and `blob:`,\\nnetwork access only to those CDNs, and no frames, workers, `<base>`, or form\\nsubmission;\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-18\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-18\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#decision\",\"content\":\"load the runner script pinned by version with Subresource Integrity by\\ndefault, and allow hosts to self-host it;\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-19\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-19\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#decision\",\"content\":\"connect over one transferred `MessagePort`; the runner accepts the connect\\nmessage only from `window.parent` and only once, and the host never listens\\nto `window` message events;\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-20\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-20\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#decision\",\"content\":\"validate every message in both directions with bounded sizes, and deliver a\\nrendered action to the host only when its type is on an allowlist;\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-21\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-21\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#decision\",\"content\":\"add a time check to every synchronous loop at transpile time, and destroy\\nand recreate the iframe when a render exceeds the host's watchdog; and\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-22\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-22\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#decision\",\"content\":\"accept theme changes only as CSS custom properties and a color scheme.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-23\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-23\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#trusted-in-page-source\",\"content\":\"Kept for reviewed code and demos, rejected for model output. Code runs with\\nthe host page's origin and can read anything the page can.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-24\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-24\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#web-worker-sandbox\",\"content\":\"Kept for computation (`sandbox-worker`), rejected for interactive UI. Workers\\nhave no DOM, so React or Preact components cannot mount there.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-25\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-25\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#dedicated-sandbox-origin\",\"content\":\"Stronger: an iframe `src` on a separate site gets its own process in browsers\\nwith site isolation, so even a loop the guard misses cannot block the host.\\nDeferred because it requires every host to operate an extra origin. The\\nprotocol does not depend on `srcdoc`, so this can be added as an option later.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-26\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-26\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#opaque-origin-srcdoc-frame\",\"content\":\"Accepted. It needs no extra infrastructure, and with loop guards and the\\nwatchdog it recovers from the failure modes generated code commonly hits.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-27\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-27\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#mcp-source-mode\",\"content\":\"`@renderify/mcp-app` renders model-written source only for apps registered with\\n`sourceMode: true`. It is off by default, and apps that do not opt in keep the\\noffline declarative contract of ADR-0001 unchanged (see its amendment).\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-28\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-28\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#mcp-source-mode\",\"content\":\"Source never runs in the view's own window. There it could post JSON-RPC to\\nthe host as the view, bypassing the tool allowlist; that design stays\\nrejected.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-29\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-29\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#mcp-source-mode\",\"content\":\"The view renders source in a nested `@renderify/frame`. The host bridge\\naccepts messages only from the view's window and the view's bridge only from\\nthe host, so content in the nested frame can address neither. Its only way\\nout is `window.renderify.action(\\\"tool:<name>\\\", args)`, which the view maps to\\n`callServerTool` when `<name>` is in `allowedTools`.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-30\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-30\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#mcp-source-mode\",\"content\":\"The view must not fetch scripts, so the runner (about 2.6 MB) travels inside\\nthe resource as a non-executing `<script type=\\\"text/plain\\\">` block. The view\\ncopies it into the frame document, and the view's CSP allows exactly that\\nscript by SHA-256 hash.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-31\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-31\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#mcp-source-mode\",\"content\":\"A `srcdoc` frame inherits the view's CSP, so source mode widens the view's\\nCSP only by what the frame needs: the runner's hash, `blob:` for transpiled\\nmodules, and the module CDNs for scripts, styles, and connections, plus\\n`blob:` images. There is still no `unsafe-eval` and no script\\n`unsafe-inline`, and frames and workers stay `'none'`. The CDNs are declared\\nin `_meta.ui.csp` (`connectDomains` and `resourceDomains`), so a host sees\\nthe wider surface before it renders anything and can refuse it.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-32\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-32\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#mcp-source-mode\",\"content\":\"Source payloads are `{ source: { code, language, runtime } }`, 256 KiB by\\ndefault. Servers refuse to return them from apps without source mode, and\\nviews without it reject them.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-33\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-33\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#mcp-source-mode\",\"content\":\"A source view's state stays in the frame. The model context only records\\nthat a source view is showing, which replaces the previous plan's state;\\ntools called through allowlisted actions carry what the server needs.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-34\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-34\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#mcp-source-mode\",\"content\":\"Verification: browser tests drive the view with the official `AppBridge`\\nunder both the shell's CSP and the CSP the ext-apps reference host\\n(`examples/basic-host`) sends, which includes `frame-src 'none'`. Chromium does\\nnot apply `frame-src` to the `srcdoc` frame, the runner boots from the inlined\\ncopy, spoofed JSON-RPC from the frame reaches neither the host nor the view,\\nand only allowlisted actions call tools. Source mode has not yet been verified\\non production hosts. A host whose CSP omits `blob:` from `script-src`, blocks\\n`srcdoc` frames, or caps resource size below the runner will not render source\\nviews; the view then shows an error, and plans keep working.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-35\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-35\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#consequences\",\"content\":\"Hosts get a small host API and a self-hostable runner (about 2.6 MB with\\nBabel and the runtime). The first render of an npm-heavy component depends\\non module CDN latency.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-36\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-36\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#consequences\",\"content\":\"Rendered code can still mislead users inside its rectangle, and it can leak\\ndata it was given through module CDN request URLs. Hosts must not pass\\nsecrets into a frame.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-37\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-37\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#consequences\",\"content\":\"Work that blocks without a loop, such as one enormous synchronous call, is\\nnot interrupted by the loop guard; in browsers that share the host's thread\\nwith the frame, the watchdog cannot fire until it returns.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-38\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-38\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#follow-up\",\"content\":\"Add a dedicated sandbox origin option.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-39\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-39\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#follow-up\",\"content\":\"Verify MCP source mode on production hosts and record per-host results,\\nincluding resource size limits.\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-40\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-40\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#follow-up\",\"content\":\"Provide framework bindings (for example a React `<RenderifyFrame>`).\"}],[\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-41\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame-41\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr/0002-sandboxed-source-frame#supersedes--superseded-by\",\"content\":\"None. Complements ADR-0001.\"}],[\"/docs/adr\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"Architecture decision records\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"Documentation\",\"Project\",\"Decision records\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/adr\"}],[\"/docs/adr-0\",{\"id\":\"/docs/adr-0\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/adr\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/adr\",\"content\":\"Du