ture#dual-input-paths\",\"content\":\"Renderify supports two fundamentally different input formats:\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-62\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-62\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#path-a-structured-runtimeplan-json\",\"content\":\"The LLM generates a JSON object conforming to the RuntimePlan schema. This path provides maximum control and deterministic behavior.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-63\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-63\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#path-b-tsxjsx-source-code\",\"content\":\"The LLM generates fenced code blocks. The codegen stage extracts the source code and wraps it in a RuntimePlan with `plan.source`. The runtime then transpiles and executes the source module.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-64\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-64\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#streaming-architecture\",\"content\":\"The streaming pipeline (`renderPromptStream`) provides progressive UI updates\\nwhen the selected provider exposes `generateResponseStream()`:\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-65\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-65\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#streaming-architecture\",\"content\":\"**llm-delta** — each transport delta from the LLM is emitted as a chunk\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-66\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-66\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#streaming-architecture\",\"content\":\"**preview** — at configurable intervals, the accumulated text is parsed and rendered as a preview\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-67\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-67\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#streaming-architecture\",\"content\":\"**final** — after LLM completion, the full pipeline executes and emits the final result\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-68\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-68\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#streaming-architecture\",\"content\":\"**error** — if any stage fails, an error chunk is emitted before the exception propagates\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-69\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-69\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#streaming-architecture\",\"content\":\"Structured generation is a single-response provider contract. When it is\\nenabled, `renderPromptStream()` emits one complete `llm-delta` after that\\nresponse arrives; it does not fabricate intermediate token chunks. Disable\\nstructured output when token-by-token progress is required.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-70\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-70\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#plugin-hook-architecture\",\"content\":\"The `CustomizationEngine` provides 10 hook points that form an interception chain:\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-71\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-71\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#plugin-hook-architecture\",\"content\":\"Each hook receives the current payload and can transform it before passing to the next stage. Multiple plugins are executed in registration order.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-72\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-72\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#module-resolution-strategy\",\"content\":\"Module resolution follows a tiered approach:\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-73\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-73\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#module-resolution-strategy\",\"content\":\"**Module manifest lookup** — if the plan includes a `moduleManifest`, bare specifiers are resolved to their `resolvedUrl`\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-74\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-74\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#module-resolution-strategy\",\"content\":\"**Compatibility aliases** — built-in aliases map `react`/`react-dom` to `preact/compat`, and include pinned versions for `recharts`\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-75\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-75\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#module-resolution-strategy\",\"content\":\"**JSPM CDN resolution** — bare specifiers are resolved to `https://ga.jspm.io/npm:{specifier}`\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-76\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-76\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#module-resolution-strategy\",\"content\":\"**Fallback CDNs** — on failure, tries configured fallback bases (default: `esm.sh`)\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-77\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-77\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#module-resolution-strategy\",\"content\":\"**Asset proxying** — CSS imports become style-injection proxy modules; JSON imports become ESM default exports\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-78\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-78\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#module-resolution-strategy\",\"content\":\"Node.js builtins and unsupported schemes (`file://`, `jsr:`) are rejected deterministically.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-79\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-79\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#browser-source-execution-model\",\"content\":\"When a RuntimePlan includes a `source` module, the execution flow is:\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-80\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-80\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#browser-source-execution-model\",\"content\":\"Optional sandbox modes (`sandbox-worker`, `sandbox-iframe`,\\n`sandbox-shadowrealm`) isolate execution in a terminable Web Worker with\\nconfigurable timeouts and fail-closed behavior. The iframe and ShadowRealm names\\nremain API-compatible routing preferences; they do not execute untrusted code\\non the main thread.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-81\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-81\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#why-jspm-instead-of-bundling\",\"content\":\"JSPM provides browser-native ESM modules from npm packages without a build step. This eliminates the need for a backend compiler while giving access to the npm ecosystem. The tiered compatibility contract (guaranteed aliases + best-effort resolution) provides predictable behavior.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-82\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-82\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#why-preact-instead-of-react\",\"content\":\"Preact is \\\\~3KB (vs React's \\\\~45KB), loads faster from CDN, and provides full React API compatibility via `preact/compat`. The compatibility bridge maps all React/ReactDOM imports to Preact equivalents transparently.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-83\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-83\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#why-babel-standalone-for-transpilation\",\"content\":\"`@babel/standalone` runs entirely in the browser, supporting TypeScript and JSX without any backend. It's loaded on demand only when the plan includes source modules.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-84\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-84\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#why-security-first-execution\",\"content\":\"Every RuntimePlan passes through security checks before any code runs. This is critical because LLM output is fundamentally untrusted — the model could generate `<script>` tags, `eval()` calls, or unsafe network requests. The policy framework provides defense-in-depth at multiple levels.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture-85\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture-85\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture#why-dual-input-paths\",\"content\":\"Structured RuntimePlan JSON gives precise control for production systems. TSX/JSX code blocks are more natural for LLMs and enable richer interactivity. Supporting both paths maximizes flexibility across different LLM capabilities and use cases.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"MCP App runtime modules\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"Documentation\",\"Project\",\"Architecture\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules\"}],[\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules-0\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules-0\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules\",\"content\":\"Responsibilities, dependency direction, and trust boundaries for the MCP App package.\"}],[\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules-1\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules-1\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules#mcp-app-runtime-modules\",\"content\":\"MCP App runtime modules\"}],[\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules-2\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules-2\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules#scope\",\"content\":\"Scope\"}],[\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules-3\",{\"id\":\"/docs/architecture/mcp-app-runtime-modules-3\",\"page_id\":\"/doc