1\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-41\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#4-strategy-over-convention\",\"content\":\"4\\\\. Strategy over Convention\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-42\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-42\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#5-zero-configuration-react-compatibility\",\"content\":\"5\\\\. Zero-Configuration React Compatibility\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-43\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-43\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#conclusion\",\"content\":\"Conclusion\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-44\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-44\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#renderify-a-runtime-engine-for-rendering-llm-generated-ui-instantly-in-the-browser\",\"content\":\"Repo: github.com/webllm/renderify\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-45\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-45\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#introduction\",\"content\":\"As large language models (LLMs) advance rapidly, AI can now generate structurally complete and logically sound UI code. Yet a key engineering question remains open: &#x2A;*how do you safely and efficiently render LLM-generated UI directly in the browser — without any backend compilation or deployment pipeline?**\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-46\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-46\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#introduction\",\"content\":\"Existing approaches each have limitations: v0/Bolt.new rely on a full Next.js compilation backend; Streamlit/Gradio are Python-based and server-rendered; Anthropic Artifacts is closed-source and non-embeddable; Sandpack/WebContainers are powerful but heavyweight.\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-47\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-47\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#introduction\",\"content\":\"Agent protocols are a different layer. MCP Apps standardizes how MCP servers ship UI into hosts, AG-UI standardizes events between agents and frontends, and A2UI lets agents compose UI from a client's trusted component catalog. Renderify complements them as a renderer: plans travel over any of these channels, and Renderify validates and renders them, or runs model-written JSX in a sandboxed frame.\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-48\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-48\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#introduction\",\"content\":\"**Renderify** was built to fill this gap. It is a runtime-first dynamic rendering engine that transpiles, sandboxes, and renders LLM-generated JSX/TSX (or structured JSON plans) directly in the browser as interactive UI — with zero build steps, zero server-side compilation, and zero deployment pipeline.\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-49\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-49\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#industry-landscape-as-of-2026-02-16\",\"content\":\"Before discussing Renderify's differentiation, it helps to establish a common framework. The diagram below breaks the \\\"LLM → UI\\\" path into six stages:\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-50\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-50\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#industry-landscape-as-of-2026-02-16\",\"content\":\"Definitions:\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-51\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-51\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#industry-landscape-as-of-2026-02-16\",\"content\":\"**Open Source**: Whether the core SDK/runtime has public source code (the platform service itself may be closed-source).\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-52\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-52\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#industry-landscape-as-of-2026-02-16\",\"content\":\"**Embeddable**: Whether it can be integrated as a capability into your own application, rather than used only within the vendor's hosted product.\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-53\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-53\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#industry-landscape-as-of-2026-02-16\",\"content\":\"**Stages Covered**: Represents the typical primary path, not the full capability boundary.\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-54\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-54\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#industry-landscape-as-of-2026-02-16\",\"content\":\"Solution\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-55\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-55\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#industry-landscape-as-of-2026-02-16\",\"content\":\"Stages Covered (typical)\"}],[\"/docs/a