ePlan is the core contract of the entire system, serving as a stable interface between all pipeline stages. Regardless of the LLM's output format, everything is normalized into a RuntimePlan before flowing through security checks, runtime execution, and UI rendering.\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-142\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-142\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#dual-input-paths\",\"content\":\"Renderify supports two fundamentally different input formats, both of which converge at the same security check and execution pipeline:\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-143\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-143\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#dual-input-paths\",\"content\":\"**Path A: Structured RuntimePlan JSON**\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-144\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-144\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#dual-input-paths\",\"content\":\"The LLM generates a structured RuntimePlan directly via JSON Schema constraints. This path offers maximum control and deterministic behavior, making it ideal for production systems.\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-145\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-145\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#dual-input-paths\",\"content\":\"**Path B: TSX/JSX Source Code**\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-146\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-146\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#dual-input-paths\",\"content\":\"The LLM generates free-form text containing code blocks. The code generation stage extracts the source code and wraps it as a RuntimePlan with a `source` field; the runtime then transpiles and executes it.\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-147\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-147\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#dual-input-paths\",\"content\":\"This dual-path design maximizes flexibility — structured JSON suits scenarios that demand precise control, while TSX/JSX code blocks feel more natural for LLMs and can express richer interactive logic.\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-148\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-148\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#security-defense-in-depth\",\"content\":\"When LLMs generate code, security is paramount. An LLM may produce `<script>` tags, `eval()` calls, or unsafe network requests. Renderify employs multiple independent defense layers, enforcing strict security policies before any code executes.\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-149\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-149\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#three-security-profiles\",\"content\":\"Policy\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-150\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-150\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#three-security-profiles\",\"content\":\"Strict\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-151\",{\"id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-151\",\"page_id\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical#three-security-profiles\",\"content\":\"Balanced (default)\"}],[\"/docs/articles/renderify-technical-152\"